35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The late-turn pool is empty. Overtime covers everything. We have no spare capacity for new night services.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The mid-city runs are slow, but the platforms clear fast. The bottleneck is waiting, not crowding.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The capital ledger is ring-fenced. The operating subsidy is trimmed. We cannot fund new infrastructure from this.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,The accessibility programme finished on time. The lane-priority stretches failed. We must trust the proven paths.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The pre-war shells are traps. Bidders price heavy contingency. The joint operators never agreed on data terms.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, if the money is gone, we cannot hire. My rosters confirm we are already stretched to breaking.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, if we can't hire, we can't extend hours. But the journey audits show waiting is the real cost.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, waiting is a symptom. The cause is the empty ledger. We must choose a plan that costs less to run.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Jonathan, the data terms are a dead end. The ferry and rail back offices are stuck. We must avoid integration.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, precisely. The committee minutes show no agreement. Any plan requiring their sign-off will stall.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, I agree. We need a plan that uses existing crews. The maintenance contract has spare capacity for lifts.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, spare capacity for lifts? That sounds like station upgrades. But do they solve the waiting time?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, station upgrades are capital intensive. The ledger is empty. We need a plan that fits the operating budget.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the pilots from eight years ago show the late-evening timetable met its cost target. It is a proven model.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the late-evening pilot worked, but the rosters are thin. Can we actually staff it now?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, the rosters are thin, but the maintenance contract has spare crew. Station upgrades use that spare capacity.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, if station upgrades use spare capacity, they are feasible. But do they reduce the waiting time I found?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, station upgrades are expensive. But the ticketing fees are high. A fare platform might save money long-term.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the fare platform requires data agreement. The committee minutes show that is impossible. We must avoid it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, agreed. The data terms are a trap. We must choose a plan that does not require the joint operators.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
