60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"The candidates are here. A is Night Service, B is Bus Corridor, C is Station Access, D is Fare Platform.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Takumi,,I see. Let us look at the data. A needs rosters we don't have. D needs data we can't get.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A and D are expensive. B and C are capital projects. The ledger is empty, but the maintenance contract has spare capacity.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Servas,,C is Station Access. The completion records show accessibility projects finish on time. The pilots show late-evening works.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"C is Station Access. The contingency pricing is high for pre-war shells, but the joint operators are not involved.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, C uses the spare maintenance capacity. A requires new rosters. I cannot support A.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, C doesn't solve the waiting time. But B is a bus corridor. The timed runs show the mid-city is slow.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, B is a bus corridor. The paving rates are high. The ticketing fees are high. C is cheaper to maintain.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, C is the proven path. The accessibility programme succeeded. The lane-priority stretches failed.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, C avoids the joint operators. The committee minutes show they are stuck. C is the only safe path.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, C is the only plan that fits our staffing reality. The maintenance contract has spare crew for lifts.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, I agree. C is feasible. B is risky. A is impossible. D is a dead end.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, C is the most balanced choice. It respects the budget and the staffing. I vote for C.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, C is the enduring path. It honors the hands we possess. I vote for C.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, C is the only choice supported by the evidence. It avoids the invisible bottlenecks. I vote for C.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, I agree. C is the most sustainable choice. I vote for C.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, I agree. C is the safest bet. It uses the stable sites and avoids the broken equipment. I vote for C.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the data is unanimous. C is the only rational choice. I vote for C.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, your caution is well-placed. C is the only path that respects our current reality. I vote for C.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the data is unanimous. C is the only rational choice. I vote for C.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
